From: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0028] regulator/sensorhub: add regulator_force_enable() and make the MCU cold-cycle symmetric

The deployed 0025 cold-cycle is ONE-WAY on beyond2lte.  vdd_mcu_1p8
(LDO21M) carries the DT regulator-always-on property, so per-handle
always_on is set and regulator_enable()/regulator_is_enabled() become
no-op/always-1.  regulator_force_disable() drops the rail but there is
no matching force-enable, so echo 1 > mcu_power cannot re-raise it; only
a full reboot restores power (confirmed on hardware).

Add regulator_force_enable() (symmetric partner of force_disable) and
use it in both power-cycle paths (set_mcu_power case 1 and 0023's
nuxel_ssp_bringup_hw fallback).

Signed-off-by: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
---
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/core.c b/drivers/regulator/core.c
index 7b56ce737141..093f02c88e00 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/core.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/core.c
@@ -2396,6 +2396,38 @@ int regulator_force_disable(struct regulator *regulator)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(regulator_force_disable);
 
+/**
+ * regulator_force_enable - force enable regulator output
+ * @regulator: regulator source
+ *
+ * Forcibly enable the regulator output voltage or current, even for a
+ * regulator whose per-handle always_on flag makes a normal regulator_enable()
+ * a no-op.  This is the symmetric partner of regulator_force_disable(); it
+ * exists so a bounded, supervised power-cycle can be completed by following a
+ * regulator_force_disable() with a regulator_force_enable() that physically
+ * re-raises the rail back to its pre-cycle (enabled) state.
+ *
+ * NOTE: this will enable the regulator output even if other consumers are
+ * disabled.  Only call it from an explicit recovery path immediately after a
+ * regulator_force_disable() on the same regulator.
+ */
+int regulator_force_enable(struct regulator *regulator)
+{
+	struct regulator_dev *rdev = regulator->rdev;
+	int ret;
+
+	mutex_lock(&rdev->mutex);
+	ret = _regulator_do_enable(rdev);
+	mutex_unlock(&rdev->mutex);
+
+	if (rdev->supply)
+		while (rdev->open_count--)
+			regulator_enable(rdev->supply);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(regulator_force_enable);
+
 static void regulator_disable_work(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct regulator_dev *rdev = container_of(work, struct regulator_dev,
